# AI Image Classifier

A simple image classification project built with Python and TensorFlow using the Fashion MNIST dataset.

## Project Overview

This project trains a neural network to classify clothing images into one of 10 categories, including:

- T-shirt/top
- Trouser
- Pullover
- Dress
- Coat
- Sandal
- Shirt
- Sneaker
- Bag
- Ankle boot

The model was trained using 60,000 images and tested on 10,000 unseen images.

## Results

The model achieved approximately:

- Training accuracy: 91%
- Test accuracy: 88%

The model is also able to return a predicted clothing category and a confidence score for each image.

## Technologies Used

- Python
- TensorFlow
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Google Colab

## How It Works

1. Load the Fashion MNIST dataset
2. Normalize the image data
3. Build a neural network using TensorFlow
4. Train the model
5. Evaluate it using unseen test data
6. Make predictions on individual images
7. Display predictions and confidence scores

## Model Architecture

The neural network contains:

- Flatten layer
- Dense layer with 128 neurons and ReLU activation
- Output layer with 10 neurons and Softmax activation

